<http://www.spektrix.com/improvcentrevancouver/event/79401APRHQVPJKKNLDNGKTCMQNHKTLSVR>
  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "Murder Is A Drag: Rhinestones Are Forever";
  schema:description """
	<h1>It's the wedding of the year, and you're invited!</h1><span><br/></span>Rhinestones are Forever: a musical murder mystery where the suspects are all drag performers. The mystery unfolds during a wedding and reception – can you help the detective solve the murder? The world’s greatest detective, Sherlock Holmo, needs your help to solve the case.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>This is a scripted interactive show and some guests will be offered roles in the wedding party. Participation is always optional, you can also choose to sit back and enjoy the show. Every ticket includes the 90 minute show, along with puzzles to solve and the chance to win prizes.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Minors are welcome at this special Sunday matinee, but must be accompanied by an adult.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>It's the wedding of the year and you're invited! Don't miss this one-of-a-kind murder mystery experience only available created by Vancouver Mysteries<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Run time: 90 minutes including intermission<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">DETECTIVE</span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Dandy</span> (@<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://instagram.com/dandyandfriends\">dandyandfriends</a>) is Murder is a Drag's world's greatest detective, Sherlock Holmo. An award-winning host, you can also catch him regularly on stage in his shows in Vancouver, hosting shows all over Metro Vancouver, or touring between LA and New York City. Or check out Dandy's Emmy-winning series <span class=\"ItalicText\">Dandyland</span> (streaming on Optik TV).<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">SUSPECTS</span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Glimmer Rouge</span> (<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://www.instagram.com/glimmerrouge/\">@glimmerrouge</a>)is a drag performer, producer and community fundraiser currently serving as Empress 54 of Vancouver. She is passionate about using drag as a joyful way to bring people together in support of meaningful causes. <span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Justin Abit</span> (<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://www.instagram.com/justin.abit.dragking/\">@justin.abit.dragking</a>) was a semi-finalist on the drag reality show <span class=\"ItalicText\">Call Me Mother</span> and performs all over BC, including everywhere from Kamloops to Haida Gwaii. Justin Abit asks us to be kind, be curious and be shiny.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Queen Kong</span> (<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://www.instagram.com/queenkongroar/\">@queenkongroar</a>) is a lifelong performer with a passion for dance and storytelling who appears in all four chapters in the Murder is a Drag series. She brings the energy of a showgirl, the attitude of a leading lady, and just enough chaos to keep audiences guessing. <span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">HOSTS</span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Tanya Bennett</span> (<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://www.instagram.com/eastvan_t/\">@eastvan_t</a>) is the scriptwriter, puzzle designer and Murder is a Drag's original host as well as the owner of Vancouver Mysteries. She is thrilled to return to co-host this special show at the Improv Centre.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Jenny Bonnycastle</span> (<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://www.instagram.com/jennybonnycastle/\">@jennybonnycastle</a>) is the Stage Manager for all Murder is a Drag shows as well as a Host (when she is not performing in a show - she is also one of the original cast members). Jenny is also the Creative Director of Crossroads Cabaret in Maple Ridge.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Murder is a Drag 3: Rhinestones Are Forever</span> is a Guest Presentation of <span class=\"BoldText\">Vancouver Mysteries</span>.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Vancouver Mysteries has been Rainbow Registered since 2021. This is a 2SLGBTQI+ friendly event, accredited through Rainbow Registered.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Rated: 🌶️🌶️🌶️ Best for teens and up. <span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Please Note: as The Improv Centre is a licensed facility, all minors (persons under the age of 19) must be accompanied by an adult.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>This show is a guest production. Special Show – Restricted. Vouchers and other discounts do not apply.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\"></span><span class=\"BoldText\"></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\"></span><span class=\"BoldText\"></span><span><br/></span>
""";
  schema:startDate "2026-11-15T13:30:00"^^xsd:dateTime;
  schema:image <https://system.spektrix.com/improvcentrevancouver/files/1624d873-2d92-49fb-9043-8ac5f08a9af4.jpg>;
  schema:location <https://spektrix.com/improvcentrevancouver/location/603AMBLCJQMLRJDMDQKBNHDKQPPDPCQLJ>;
  schema:organizer <https://spektrix.com/improvcentrevancouver/organization/the-improv-centre>;
  schema:url <https://theimprovcentre.ca/shows/>;
  schema:offers _:1ffe682b6d774e17985871fde78009e76744;
  schema:duration "PT90M";
  schema:endDate "2026-11-15T15:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime .

