<http://www.spektrix.com/improvcentrevancouver/event/83403ADMHLRTQPVCRNKVRCMQQSDGQBBKH>
  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "The Heat Workshops 2027";
  schema:description """
	Workshop #1: 10:30am-1pm<span><br/></span><h1><span class=\"BoldText\">Working with a muso: Musical Improv! taught by Kid Jesties</span></h1><span class=\"BoldText\">Duration</span>: 2.5hrs<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Workshop Level:</span> Intermediate (Improv 103 or higher)<span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">Any questions about experience or eligibility please reach out to education@theimprovcentre.ca</span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Price: </span>$75<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">About:</span> Musical improvisers can add a huge amount to scenes via live scoring, especially in building stories and characters that have a lot of heart and emotion. In New Zealand almost every show is underscored by a live musician who is highly skilled at leading and supporting scenes, as well as the more traditional format of building improvised musicals. This workshop will provide improvisers with the opportunity to play scenes and perform with a professional live scoring improv artist and learn how to be influenced by external inputs while performing .<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Workshop #2: 1:15pm-3:15pm<span><br/></span><h1><span class=\"BoldText\">What’s That You’re Holding?: Environment and Space Object Improv taught by Kolliflower</span></h1><span class=\"BoldText\">Duration:</span> 2hrs<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Workshop Level:</span> Intermediate (Improv 102 or equivalent)<span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">Any questions about experience or eligibility please reach out to education@theimprovcentre.ca</span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Price:</span> $60<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">About:</span> Have you ever been in an improv scene and been handed a cup of coffee that mysteriously disappears after the first sip? Have you ever painstakingly set the dining table to have someone else walk right through it? But most importantly, have you ever been in a scene and thought “there must be something better to do than just stand and talk”? Well, this workshop is for you. Learn how to move through your scenes with intention, create and use objects with purpose, and bring your environment to life.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Workshop #3: 3:30pm-5:30pm<span><br/></span><h1><span class=\"BoldText\">The Next Best Thing: Expanding your improv choices taught by SPIT</span></h1><span class=\"BoldText\">Duration: </span>2hrs<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Workshop Level:</span> Intermediate (Improv 103 or higher)<span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">Any questions about experience or eligibility please reach out to education@theimprovcentre.ca</span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Price: </span>$60<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">About:</span> In this workshop, discover different ways to break free from what you're used to and explore improv paths you rarely take. Be inspired by improv principles: obvious/non-obvious, and 'use everything', and maybe you'll see that the next best thing might just be the best choice.<span><br/></span>
""";
  schema:startDate "2027-01-30T10:30:00"^^xsd:dateTime;
  schema:location <https://spektrix.com/improvcentrevancouver/location/603AMBLCJQMLRJDMDQKBNHDKQPPDPCQLJ>;
  schema:organizer <https://spektrix.com/improvcentrevancouver/organization/the-improv-centre>;
  schema:url <https://theimprovcentre.ca/shows/>;
  schema:duration "PT60M";
  schema:endDate "2027-01-30T11:30:00"^^xsd:dateTime .

<http://www.spektrix.com/improvcentrevancouver/event/83404ASBVTPTMVBVGLMCCDLRQRSGTQCBJ>
  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "The Heat Workshops 2027";
  schema:description """
	Workshop #1: 10:30am-1pm<span><br/></span><h1><span class=\"BoldText\">Working with a muso: Musical Improv! taught by Kid Jesties</span></h1><span class=\"BoldText\">Duration</span>: 2.5hrs<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Workshop Level:</span> Intermediate (Improv 103 or higher)<span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">Any questions about experience or eligibility please reach out to education@theimprovcentre.ca</span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Price: </span>$75<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">About:</span> Musical improvisers can add a huge amount to scenes via live scoring, especially in building stories and characters that have a lot of heart and emotion. In New Zealand almost every show is underscored by a live musician who is highly skilled at leading and supporting scenes, as well as the more traditional format of building improvised musicals. This workshop will provide improvisers with the opportunity to play scenes and perform with a professional live scoring improv artist and learn how to be influenced by external inputs while performing .<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Workshop #2: 1:15pm-3:15pm<span><br/></span><h1><span class=\"BoldText\">What’s That You’re Holding?: Environment and Space Object Improv taught by Kolliflower</span></h1><span class=\"BoldText\">Duration:</span> 2hrs<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Workshop Level:</span> Intermediate (Improv 102 or equivalent)<span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">Any questions about experience or eligibility please reach out to education@theimprovcentre.ca</span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Price:</span> $60<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">About:</span> Have you ever been in an improv scene and been handed a cup of coffee that mysteriously disappears after the first sip? Have you ever painstakingly set the dining table to have someone else walk right through it? But most importantly, have you ever been in a scene and thought “there must be something better to do than just stand and talk”? Well, this workshop is for you. Learn how to move through your scenes with intention, create and use objects with purpose, and bring your environment to life.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Workshop #3: 3:30pm-5:30pm<span><br/></span><h1><span class=\"BoldText\">The Next Best Thing: Expanding your improv choices taught by SPIT</span></h1><span class=\"BoldText\">Duration: </span>2hrs<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Workshop Level:</span> Intermediate (Improv 103 or higher)<span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">Any questions about experience or eligibility please reach out to education@theimprovcentre.ca</span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Price: </span>$60<span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">About:</span> In this workshop, discover different ways to break free from what you're used to and explore improv paths you rarely take. Be inspired by improv principles: obvious/non-obvious, and 'use everything', and maybe you'll see that the next best thing might just be the best choice.<span><br/></span>
""";
